From af310eab7a66353c92f07fac7b06a1fe93971985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tao Xiaobai <1599170798@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:15:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Little Craft Launcher: end a preparation by its real
 completion, not by progress records

The preparation waited for the runtime's progress keeper to be idle before
releasing its lock and reporting. A Java download that fails after receiving
data (read timeout) leaves its progress record registered although the
download thread has ended, so that wait never returned: no failed/cancelled
was reported and every later preparation was refused until the app was killed.

- LclPreparation: asynchronous work is started through Tasks and the
  preparation waits for those Futures, on every path. Progress records are no
  longer consulted, neither there nor before starting the game.
- LclProgress.clearing: the synchronous Java step can no longer leave its
  record behind, whether it returns or throws.
- Regressions with the runtime's real downloader, progress wrapper and
  progress keeper against a server that stalls mid-archive: the record is
  registered, the read timeout ends the work, failed (or cancelled, when the
  user had left) is reported, no record remains, a retry prepares normally;
  plus the existing blocked-child cases, now on real Futures.
